    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic center houses San Luis Fortress, the city’s first banks, and the Santiago Apostol Cathedral.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santiago_de_los_Caballeros"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "On a hill overlooking Santiago stands a 67‑meter marble monument, the city’s tallest structure.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santiago_de_los_Caballeros"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Museo del Tabaco displays tobacco manufacturing methods and the crop’s influence on Santiago’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santiago_de_los_Caballeros"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Santiago hosts universities like O&M and a Binational Cultural Center founded by Dominicans and Americans in 1962.",
